  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Separate trust and authority",
      "items": [
        "Browser JWT session authenticates a user; optional inference Bearer keys remain backend-only.",
        "Tunnel transports traffic. Bearer proxy is access control, not a complete sandbox; its method/path allowlist is unknown here.",
        "Model output is evidence. The deterministic backend engine and application transaction own decision writes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Auth and Judge Demo data",
      "items": [
        "Auth application code stores versions, private attachments/hashes, AI runs, decisions and audit in PostgreSQL.",
        "Judge Demo uses Mock VLM and separate SQLite; Render root config is ephemeral. Verify uses in-memory SQLite per case in the same process (see Verify diagram).",
        "The Mock and Verify paths do not connect to Ollama."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Configuration is not deployment evidence · 2026-10-17",
      "items": [
        "Root Render config describes Judge Demo. Auth staging is a separate Blueprint and is not proof of a live service.",
        "Auth staging sets LOCAL_VLM_ALLOW_REMOTE=false; .env.example leaves endpoint and keys blank.",
        "No proxy source/config, tunnel config, origin transport, Ollama target or current live inference was verified."
      ]
    }
  ]
